{
  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case05",
  "description": "A negative category balance, which truncates TOWARDS ZERO and carries its sign as an overpunch. TRAN-CAT-BAL is S9(09)V99 - signed - and -1000.00 at 12.50 has an exact quotient of -10.41666..., so the store at :464-465 keeps -10.41 and not -10.42. The seeded balance's trailing byte is }, the negative-zero overpunch, and TRAN-AMT's is J, which is a negative one: the sign travels in the trailing byte of the zoned span in both directions, and a codec that read the span as text would lose it in both. This is also the case that proves truncation is not the same as flooring - flooring -10.41666... would give -10.42, one cent further from zero, and that value appears nowhere in this gate. The account is acctdata.txt row 0 verbatim, so the 12.50 rate sits under the 'DEFAULT' group and the two :418-419 lines are displayed; the arithmetic is identical either way, which is why the lookup path is allowed to be the ordinary one here.",
